{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172069-the-old-gods","id":1172069,"title":"The Old Gods?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-31T14:20:03-08:00","id":1172069,"title":"The Old Gods?","content":"I'm just rereading Seers of the Throne for a game I hope to run in the new year (Does anyone happen to know why you can only buy this book and the Chroniclers Guide as PDF on Drivethru? I'd love to have a print copy.,..), and I stumbled over the sidebar on page 39, titled &quot;The Old Gods&quot;. It mentioned that some of the exiled Old Gods exist today on the material plane - was there ever anything else on that somewhere in one of the other books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T14:45:05-08:00","id":1172074,"title":"","content":"They are the Bound, mostly. Supernal entities that were enslaved/tossed out into the Fallen. If you're talking Old God Old God, then you need to come up with a rank 6 Supernal Entity and stick it into the plot somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T14:45:51-08:00","id":1172075,"title":"","content":"Typically, they're the Bound. There's also a faction of arch-mages that seek to return them to the Supernal and in so doing get hoovered into ascension along with the god they boost back into their thrones. That faction can be found in the Imperial Mysteries book. If you want to see a Bound in action you can check out the AP called Soul Cage that DaveB ran a while back. It's 1e, but the overall ideas are still gold standard. I imagine that there will also be some information that will be relevant when Signs of Sorcery comes out as part of the book is meant to deal with Supernal things that, while Supernal, are outside the ability of Mages to comprehend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}